"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":48,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"## Report — fw-7al\n\n**Bead:** fw-7al (P1 bug) — doctor checked that `.claude/settings.json` exists, not that it grants anything. Ran **solo** per `run-context.json`, so no blackbird registration or reservation.\n\n**What I did** (3 commits on `bead/fw-7al`):\n- New `tools/fleet/settingsprobe.go`: parses `permissions.allow`/`deny`/`defaultMode` and requires each capability flywheel-next invokes — `bd`, `guard.sh`, `Write`, `Edit`, `git add/commit/push`, `gh pr create`, and the language's test runner. Reports **per missing capability**. Rule matching mirrors the runner (bare tool, `prefix:*`, exact, deny beats allow); for Write/Edit only bare rules count, so `Edit(.claude/**)` denies stay a guard and `Write(src/**)` is not a grant.\n- Added `.claude/settings.json` to the manifest so absent/gitignored is a Finding; the probe runs only on a tracked file, and it runs under CI too so `drift.yml` catches it weekly.\n- Tests: powerless-but-present (the shipped case, both unit and full-parity `Diagnose`), plus absent, invalid JSON, one-short, deny semantics, scoped rules, `defaultMode`, per-language runner, untracked file.\n\n**Gate:** pre-commit (identity, replay-guard, gofmt, beads, vet, conformance, full tests) green on every commit; `go test ./...` green; push-guard passed.\n\n**Review (ADR 0013):** 3 lenses, 13 findings in the ledger — 6 accepted and fixed (the scoped-deny bug was flagged by two lenses), 2 ignored, 5 rejected with reasons.\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel/pull/77 — weight `w:2`, bead noted and audit-logged. Bead left open until merge.\n\n**Left out:** `*` globs inside Bash specs read as literal (fail-closed, ponytail-commented); Python runners are `uv run pytest`/`pytest` only — if spotify's gate is named differently, `testRunners` is the one-line upgrade. I could not run `fleet doctor -self` by hand (binary not in the allowlist), but the \"real file\" test row exercises the probe against this repo's actual `settings.json`.","ttft_ms":3386,"type":"result","duration_ms":567297,"uuid":"b3b39ccf-601c-4a3d-99e8-0b34f1ce0d50","ttft_stream_ms":2720,"time_to_request_ms":118,"queued_turn_count":0}
